@Okane.Api_HostAddress = http://localhost:5091

# Run these requests top-to-bottom, in order, with the REST Client extension (or any client that
# keeps a cookie jar across requests). Auth is cookie-based: Login sets the "okane_access_token"
# HttpOnly cookie, and every request after it is authenticated automatically via that cookie - no
# Authorization header needed. Steps 6-8 reference the wallet ids captured from step 5's response,
# so step 5 must run before them.
#
# Re-running from the top a second time will fail at Register (email already registered, 409) -
# either change the email below or just start again from Login.

### 1. Register a new user
# @name register
POST {{Okane.Api_HostAddress}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Dashboard Demo",
  "email": "dashboard.demo@example.com",
  "password": "DemoPass123"
}

### 2. Log in - sets the auth cookie used by every request below
# @name login
POST {{Okane.Api_HostAddress}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "dashboard.demo@example.com",
  "password": "DemoPass123"
}

### 3. List wallets - registration auto-creates an "External Wallet" for the new user
GET {{Okane.Api_HostAddress}}/api/wallets

### 4. Create a standard wallet to transact against
# @name createWallet
POST {{Okane.Api_HostAddress}}/api/wallets
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Checking"
}

### 5. List wallets again - newest first, so items[0] is "Checking" and items[1] is "External Wallet"
# @name listWallets
GET {{Okane.Api_HostAddress}}/api/wallets

### 6. Record income: External Wallet -> Checking (Salary)
POST {{Okane.Api_HostAddress}}/api/transactions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fromWalletId": "{{listWallets.response.body.$.details.items[1].id}}",
  "toWalletId": "{{listWallets.response.body.$.details.items[0].id}}",
  "amount": 2000.00,
  "description": "Salary"
}

### 7. Record income: External Wallet -> Checking (Refund)
POST {{Okane.Api_HostAddress}}/api/transactions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fromWalletId": "{{listWallets.response.body.$.details.items[1].id}}",
  "toWalletId": "{{listWallets.response.body.$.details.items[0].id}}",
  "amount": 150.00,
  "description": "Refund"
}

### 8. Record expense: Checking -> External Wallet (Rent)
POST {{Okane.Api_HostAddress}}/api/transactions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fromWalletId": "{{listWallets.response.body.$.details.items[0].id}}",
  "toWalletId": "{{listWallets.response.body.$.details.items[1].id}}",
  "amount": 85.50,
  "description": "Rent"
}

### 9. List transactions (paginated) to confirm everything was recorded
GET {{Okane.Api_HostAddress}}/api/transactions?page=1&pageSize=20

### 10. Generate the dashboard report for the current month
GET {{Okane.Api_HostAddress}}/api/dashboard
